# Frontend rules

- Read [docs/DESIGN.md](../../docs/DESIGN.md) before editor, library, or settings layout changes.
- Reuse components under `components/shared/`, `components/editor/`, `components/library/`.
- Import icons only via `components/shared/Icon.tsx`; register new names in `icon-registry.ts`.
- Use tokens from `lib/surface-colors.ts`, `lib/button-styles.ts`, `lib/panel-chrome.ts` — avoid one-off hex values.
- Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` only for interactivity, Fabric.js, or browser APIs.
- Preserve accessibility: labels, `aria-*`, keyboard behavior on menus and dialogs.
- Portaled UI (modals, dropdowns) should use `createPortal(..., document.body)` when panels clip content.
- Keep responsive behavior on settings tabs and library grid.
- Do not refactor unrelated UI in the same task.
- After UI changes: run dev server, visually verify, check browser console for errors.
